 "standard_text": "Solve equations by inspection, trial and improvement or algebraic processes (additive and multiplicative inverses, and factorisation); solve equations of the form: a product of factors = 0; solve equations using laws of exponents; use substitution in equations to generate tables of ordered pairs.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 9 algebraic equations worksheets: linear equations, equations by factorisation, exponential equations and formulae. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Make one side 0, factorise, each factor = 0.",
 "key_sub": "Same base: equate the exponents.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Linear equations: expand, collect like terms, then solve.</li><li>Equations by factorisation: make one side 0, factorise, then each factor = 0.</li><li>x² − 5x + 6 = 0 → (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0 → x = 2 or x = 3.</li><li>Exponential equations: write both sides with the same base. 3ˣ = 81 = 3⁴, so x = 4.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>x² = 7x</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x² − 7x = 0</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x(x − 7) = 0</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x = 0 or x = 7</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dividing by x</td><td>You lose the solution x = 0.</td></tr><tr><td>One solution only</td><td>Each factor gives a solution.</td></tr><tr><td>One side only</td><td>Multiply both sides by the denominator.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 9 say about equations?",
